==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*freh-, *freg-'', from Indo-European {{proto|Indo-European|preḱ-|to ask|lang=ang}}.

Cognate with Old Saxon ''[[fregnan]]'', Old Norse ''[[fregna]]'', Gothic '''[[𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌹𐌷𐌽𐌰𐌽]]''', and related to Old High German {{term|fraga|frāga|lang=goh}} (German ''[[Frage]]'').  The Indo-European root also gave Old Persian ''aparsam'' ‘I asked’{{rfscript|Cuneiform}}, Irish ''[[arco]]'', Welsh ''[[archaf]]'', Armenian {{term|հարց||tr=harc'|lang=hy}}, Tocharian A ''prak-'', Tocharian B ''prek-''{{rfscript|Tocharian}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfrijnɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=III|head=friġnan}} (''third-person singular present'' '''[[frigneþ|friġneþ]]''', ''third-person singular preterite'' '''[[frægn|fræġn]]''', ''preterite plural'' '''[[frugnon|fruġnon]]''', ''past participle'' ('''ġe''')'''[[frugnen|fruġnen]]''')

# to [[ask]], [[pray]]

